<h2>Situations at a glance</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>What the guarantee says</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>A ticket is not valid or not what you ordered</td><td>Tickets will be authentic and valid for entry, and you receive the tickets you ordered or better. Contact us and we work with the seller to make it right.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Tickets do not arrive</td><td>Tickets will be shipped in time for at least one delivery attempt before the event. Contact us as soon as you notice.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The event is canceled</td><td>A full refund, delivery fees excluded.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The event is rescheduled</td><td>Tickets typically stay valid for the new date.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>You change your mind</td><td>Tickets are not refundable for a change of plans. Check the event and price before you order.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Because every order depends on the event, the seller and the delivery method, read the <a href="/terms-and-conditions">terms and conditions</a> too. If you are not sure whether your situation qualifies, ask before the event date.</p>

<h2>Prices and resale</h2>
<p>Seat Outlet is a resale marketplace, so ticket prices are set by sellers and can be above or below face value. The guarantee protects the order, not the price, so compare listings before you buy. Our <a href="/why-are-concert-tickets-so-expensive">guide to ticket prices</a> explains what moves them. When a refund applies, timing depends on the seller and the payment provider, so we cannot give a fixed number of days.</p>

<h2>If something goes wrong</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Check your order confirmation email for your order and delivery details.</li>
  <li>If something looks wrong, contact <a href="/ticket-customer-service">customer service</a> as soon as you notice, and well before the event.</li>
  <li>Have your order number and event details ready.</li>
  <li>Keep any messages and screenshots in case we need them.</li>
</ol>
<p>You can also email <a href="mailto:support@seatoutlet.com">support@seatoutlet.com</a> or check the <a href="/ticket-faq">ticket FAQ</a>. The FTC shares <a href="https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/online-shopping" target="_blank" rel="noopener">tips on shopping online safely</a>.</p>

